<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis-Joseph de Montcalm</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1712–1759</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Marquis de Montcalm</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis-Joseph de Montcalm was a French general who commanded the French army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a> from 1756. He took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-oswego">Fort Oswego</a> in 1756 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-william-henry">Fort William Henry</a> in 1757 and won a notable defensive victory at Carillon in 1758. He was mortally wounded at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-plains-of-abraham">Battle of the Plains of Abraham</a> outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> on 13 September 1759 and died the next day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-joseph-de-montcalm.jpg" alt="Louis-Joseph de Montcalm" width="320" height="360" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antoine Louis François Sergent dit Sergent-Marceau · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis-Joseph_de_Montcalm_cph.3g09407.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
